 "method": "LO (DDO) certificate V002 (successor of certificates_v001 lo_cert_c2v001.py / gates/LO_CERT_V001.json and\nLO_CERT_K128_V001.json, which stay unedited).  Root A52 (K_big ruling pending in A53; LO must reach beyond 128, CHECK F5).\nReplay only; no launch.\n\nSame object and the same absolute-bound method as V001 (its docstring, kept verbatim in the record's method_v001):\n  route-A channel only.  Components 1-9 reach a route-A row through prediction v005 (54136c71) L128-129\n  pressure_streaming_speed(d_log_N=m['dlnN_dR'], d_log_R=m['dln_sqrt_gphiphi_dR']) and the proper-volume density\n  L144-147 (slogdet g_cylindrical; jac = N exp(logdet/2)).  Route B: none -- rotation v005 uvt successor (aa9992bd) L283\n  computes metric.evaluate_point (validity guard, result unused) and L284-288 form N, Phi, Phi_R, Phi_z from f[0], g[0] only.\n  |dv_i,s| <= (v_i R_i / 4) rho_s B1_s,  rho_s = sup ||Ghat(k)||_2 4 gamma |k|^2 over the shell (points with |k|_inf > K),\n  B1_s = the module's own field-bound shell integral (int_{D cap s} |k| T_inf |S_T|), here from ONE build of the saved C4R3\n  le3 roster at O = cylinder 256 (TEST_ONLY certificates; I1-T on that state recorded).\nShells: the seven V007 shells (4,5] .. (32,64], plus (64,128], (128,256] (complete spherical shells inside cyl 256) and\n(256,363] = D cap {|k| > 256} for O = cylinder 256 (the K_big = 256 production domain; NOT the complete spherical shell;\nits outer edge 363 is the module's last unit-shell edge, ceil(sqrt2 x 256) = 363).\nrho_s two ways:  rho_sampled = V001's sampled max (52 dirs x 128/decade and 104 x 256/decade; v001 rho_shell);\nrho_envelope = sup over direction x |k| x the cardinal torus (certs2_common Envelope; dominates the actual set) by a global\ngrid (torus 12^3, 200 hemisphere directions, 3 |k| values) + batched local maximization.  max_over_tau uses\nrho_used = max(rho_sampled, rho_envelope); max_over_tau_rho_sampled (the V001 definition) is kept alongside.",
 "method_v001": "LO (DDO) and LO_NGC certificates (prereg V007 draft R1 gates LO / LO_NGC; design V002 sec 1.6, R1 L8) as replays.  No launch.\n\nObject: the omitted non-lapse tail, components 1-9 of the response x(k) = -K(k)^-1 e_n to the lapse-only tail source\n(x_0 = T; components 1-6 = delta C in Mandel order, 7-9 = delta mu), over |k| shells of D = shell \\ cube K.\n\nWhere components 1-9 can reach a row (code reading, cited):\n  * route-B rows: NOT AT ALL.  rotation v005 uvt successor L283-292 forms Phi, Phi_R, Phi_z from f[0], g[0] only; the\n    metric evaluate_point result there and in columns v005 L246 is a validity guard (N > 0, C SPD, g_phiphi > 0) whose\n    outputs are unused.  The readout-coupled share is therefore exactly 0 (structural).\n  * route A: prediction v005 L127-129 pressure_streaming_speed(d_log_N = dlnN/dR, d_log_R = dln sqrt(g_phiphi)/dR) and the\n    proper volume density L143-147 (slogdet g_cylindrical).  This is the channel measured here.\nIndicator (Claude3's unit: the linear share of a row speed in tau, shell-resolved; origin_c3v001 / shell_resolved_c4_c3v001):\n  v^2 = c^2 (dlnN/dR) / (dln sqrt g_phiphi/dR),  dln sqrt g_phiphi/dR = 1/R + d_R h/2,  h = e_phi^T Ghat e_phi,\n  Ghat = Cbar^-1/2 mat(x_1..6) Cbar^-1/2 S_T  ->  dv_i = -(v_i R_i / 4) d_R h(R_i).\n  Taken as an absolute bound (|integral| <= integral of |.|, so it bounds Claude3's signed share):\n  |dv_i,s| <= (v_i R_i / 4) rho_s B1_s,  rho_s = max_k ||Ghat(k)||_2 4 gamma |k|^2 (per unit lapse source, i.e. relative to\n  T_inf), B1_s = int_{D cap s} |k| T_inf |S_T| d^3k/(2pi)^3 (the module's own field-bound shell integrals B_s^(1), state built\n  with O = cylinder 128 so every |k| <= 128 shell is complete).  rho_s is a sampled max (52 dirs x 128/decade and 104 x\n  256/decade, points with |k|_inf > K) -> an ESTIMATE like EPS, not a proven sup.  Proper-volume channel reported:\n  |d ln sqrt det g| <= rhoV_s B0_s, rhoV_s = max |tr Ghat|/2 relative to T_inf.\nLO_NGC (saved T120L K=2 state's iteration-0 roster: stars + H2 + razor-thin HI, module tests b/f inputs; O = cylinder 16,\nNGC production quadrature): the N-test statistics read lnN = log(1 + x_0 field) only (metric v002 L76-77 N = 1 + dx[0];\nreplay_c1 lnN), so their coupling to components 1-9 is exactly 0; the record gives the field-level magnitude bound\nmax|h| <= rho_s B0_s in theta units (theta = 3.3657664138980042e-9).",
